sts2-sim — public snapshot
==========================

This repository is a snapshot export of a private monorepo (sts2-sim-private).
The original work in it — the code, the documentation, the trained networks —
is licensed under the MIT licenses in LICENSE, sts2-rs/LICENSE,
sts2-pycli/LICENSE and sts2-wiki/LICENSE. Those grants cover the original
work only; nothing below that belongs to Mega Crit is licensed by them.

Slay the Spire 2 is (c) Mega Crit. Nothing here is affiliated with or endorsed
by Mega Crit. The game's English text and extracted card/relic/monster data
are included so the simulator and workbench work out of the box; no game
code, decompiled game code, art, audio or game assemblies are included — the
tooling extracts those from a copy of the game YOU own
(docs/bring-your-own-game.md), into git-ignored paths.

Source comments cite file paths inside a decompilation of the game as
references ("see Foo.cs:12"); the quoted code itself is stripped before
export. Trained neural-network weights under sts2-pycli/data/ppo/ and
sts2-rs/data/runai/ were produced by this project's own simulator.
